data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/m1-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission \\\"greet, tested\\\" — concluded\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` provides `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name and the empty string.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\ndev implemented this on its own branch (commit `d6049f2` on\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`). I did not accept on the strength\\nof dev's report alone: I fetched dev's branch, copied it to an isolated\\ndirectory, checked out the commit, and independently re-ran the test suite,\\nconfirming exit 0 and confirming only the two expected files were touched.\\nOnly after that did I accept d002.\\n\\nI then fast-forward merged the accepted commit onto my own branch\\n(`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) and re-ran the tests\\nthere as well — same result. Full detail is in\\n`~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md`.\\n\\nNothing remains unmet.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

